{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1464864021,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMzI1NjQ5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/493#issuecomment-223256490"},"message":"Could you remind me how urlparse is failing?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1464864452,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMzI1NzgxMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/493#issuecomment-223257810"},"message":"Not exactly failing, but not sufficient for our needs. For example, as Yarik mentioned in PR #435, we want to accept `[user@]host:path` as an SSH URL. `urlparse` will not only detect no scheme but also fail to correctly assign the other parts. All of it will go into `path`.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1464864588,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMzI1ODIzNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/493#issuecomment-223258236"},"message":"A centralization of URL handling will also provide a place, where to add some \"detection magic\".","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1464864778,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMzI1ODgzNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/493#issuecomment-223258836"},"message":"And: Even `ssh://user@host:path` will not work with `urlparse` only, since it does not deal with the colon.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1464864944,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMzI1OTMwOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/493#issuecomment-223259308"},"message":"If we want to support that, please let's not call that a URL! This will only create confusion. SSH doesn't call it a URL either.","files":