or that is a ParseResult itself. Any other code else then just gets the ParseResult instead of the original string (could be done via `constraint` for example)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1464966844,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMzYwNjg1Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/493#issuecomment-223606856"},"message":"`user@host:path` would then lead to\n- `ssh://user@host/path`, which would be passed on to `urlparse`\n  or\n- `ParseResult(scheme='ssh', netloc='user@host', path='path*, ...)\n\nIn both cases an URL, that was NOT recognized as sth to do magic on, would simply be passed on to `urlparse`","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1464967680,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMzYxMDcwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/493#issuecomment-223610705"},"message":"I hope to work on #441 atm, so may be I will take a chance to provide some ultimate magical handling","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1465796876,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyNTQ5Mzk3Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/493#issuecomment-225493973"},"message":"Looks like we can close this as the merge has happended.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1465796876,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50Njg5OTg3NTgz"},"status":2}]}